Slide 1 — Title

221B — Holmes Personal Intelligence System

A Personal Scheduling & Investigation Interface for Sherlock Holmes

Include:

Your name
Student ID
Module name
Faculty / University
Date

Visual: dark Sherlock Holmes / 221B-inspired background with minimal decoration.

Slide 2 — Selected User

Sherlock Holmes

Occupation: Consulting Detective
Base: 221B Baker Street, London

Why Sherlock Holmes?

Manages multiple investigations simultaneously
Receives unexpected urgent cases
Analyses large amounts of evidence
Frequently travels between locations
Needs to make rapid decisions
Requires organised information for deductions

Design goal:

Create a system that helps Holmes manage his schedule and investigations without interrupting his reasoning process.

Slide 3 — User Profile

User Persona

Attribute	Description
Name	Sherlock Holmes
Role	Consulting Detective
Environment	London
Primary workspace	221B Baker Street
Main activities	Investigation, analysis, consultation
Technology need	Fast access to relevant information
Primary goal	Solve cases efficiently

Key characteristic:

Holmes needs information to be structured, prioritised and immediately actionable.

Slide 4 — User Problems & Limitations

Contextual Challenges

Multiple investigations at the same time
Unpredictable urgent cases
Large quantities of evidence
Competing appointments
Frequent travel
Information overload
Rapid decision-making
Difficulty distinguishing routine activities from critical events
UX Problem

How can Holmes manage a changing daily schedule while simultaneously tracking investigations and making rapid decisions?

Slide 5 — User Requirements

Functional Requirements

The system should allow Holmes to:

View today's schedule
Add and manage events
Detect schedule conflicts
View active cases
Review case details
Manage evidence
Organise deductions
Track tasks
Monitor investigation locations
Receive notifications
UX Requirements

The interface should be:

Fast
Clear
Prioritised
Consistent
Responsive
Easy to navigate
